{"step_index":759,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:03:55Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan for integrating MATLAB ANN surrogate metamodels into the platform as a real-time Digital Twin and Predictive Optimization Engine.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Digital Twin & ANN Surrogate Engine Implementation Plan\\n\\nIntegrate the user's MATLAB Artificial Neural Network (`.m`) surrogate metamodels into the platform as an interactive **Digital Twin & Real-Time Predictive Simulation Engine**.\\n\\n## User Review Required\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The MATLAB ANN models are ported directly into pure Python / NumPy with zero MATLAB runtime dependency. All mathematical operations (input scaling, 10-neuron hyperbolic tangent hidden layer, linear output layer, and reverse scaling) match the exact IEEE floating-point outputs from MATLAB Neural Network Toolbox `genFunction`.\\n\\n## Proposed Changes\\n\\n### Core Metamodel & Digital Twin Module\\n\\n#### [NEW] [ann_surrogate.py](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/ann_surrogate.py)\\n- **MATLAB `.m` AST/Regex Parser**: Parses any `genFunction` `.m` file dynamically, extracting normalization parameters (`xoffset`, `gain`, `ymin`), weight matrices (`IW1_1`, `LW2_1`), and biases (`b1`, `b2`).\\n- **Vectorized NumPy Inference Engine**: Runs single-sample or batch inference ($\\\\approx 0.05\\\\text{ms}$ latency).\\n- **Pre-configured Model Registry**:\\n  - `Model 1 Multi-Station Metamodel` (Station 1, Station 2, Station 3)\\n  - `Model 2 Multi-Station Metamodel` (Drilling, Milling, Assembly)\\n  - `Model 2 Dedicated Station Metamodels` (`Drilling`, `Milling`, `Assembly`)\\n  - `Combinatorial Cell-Station Metamodels` (`c1s2`, `c1s4`, `c2s2`, `c2s4`, `c3s2`, `c3s3`, `c4s3`, `c4s4`)\\n- **Validation Engine**: Evaluates ANN predictions against uploaded Rockwell Arena simulation logs (`Model_1.csv`, `Model_2.csv`, `Model_3.csv`) computing $R^2$, Mean Absolute Error (MAE), and Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE).\\n- **Prescriptive Optimization Solver**: Grid/gradient search finding optimal arrival rates / setpoints to maximize throughput while keeping all stations below $85\\\\%$ utilization threshold.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Charting & Visualization Upgrades\\n\\n#### [MODIFY] [chart_helpers.py](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/sc\n<truncated 1371 bytes>","Description":"\"Implementation plan for Digital Twin & ANN Surrogate Engine integration\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\win-10\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2\\\\implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing implementation plan artifact\"","toolSummary":"\"Write implementation plan\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
